1
00:04:43,333 --> 00:04:49,333
The camera never lies...

2
00:09:26,666 --> 00:09:32,666
Exhibit A is a thriller, drama, horror film directed by Dom Rotheroe.

3
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:16,000
Exhibit A tells the timely story of a normal family
disintegrating under financial pressure.

4
00:18:53,333 --> 00:18:59,333
All is not as it seems as the King family go about their
day-to-day lives oblivious of the horror to come.

5
00:23:36,666 --> 00:23:42,666
Dad Andy (Bradley Cole) is nursing a secret that ultimately
leads to terrible consequences for them all.

6
00:28:20,000 --> 00:28:26,000
We witness these chilling events unfold through daughter Judith's
video camera, which subsequently becomes Exhibit A.

7
00:33:03,333 --> 00:33:09,333
Andy King, played by Bradley Cole.

8
00:37:46,666 --> 00:37:52,666
Joe King, played by Oliver Lee.

9
00:42:30,000 --> 00:42:36,000
Judith King, played by Brittany Ashworth.

10
00:47:13,333 --> 00:47:19,333
Sheila King, played by Angela Forrest.

11
00:51:56,666 --> 00:52:02,666
Wayne, played by Jason Allen.

12
00:56:40,000 --> 00:56:46,000
Exhibit A is a 2007 British independent psychological thriller film directed
by Dom Rotheroe and produced by Darren Bender for Warp Films.

13
01:01:23,333 --> 01:01:29,333
The film is an example of the found footage genre and stars Bradley
Cole, Brittany Ashworth, Angela Forrest and Oliver Lee.

14
01:06:06,666 --> 01:06:12,666
It was filmed on location in Yorkshire and Suffolk and released
on 1 October 2007 at the Raindance Film Festival.

15
01:10:50,000 --> 01:10:56,000
It was the last film that prolific stuntman Roy Alon worked on.

16
01:15:33,333 --> 01:15:39,333
The film explores themes of espionage, family, found
footage, pseudo-documentary, faux documentary.

17
01:20:16,666 --> 01:20:22,666
The tone is dark and emotional and intense.
